      "type": "mcq",
      "question": "In Fresnel's biprism (μ = 1.5) experiment the distance between source and biprism is 0.3m and that between biprism and screen is 0.7m and angle of prism is 1°. The fringe width with light of wavelength 6000 Å will be",
      "options": [
        "1 cm",
        "0.011 cm",
        "2 cm",
        "4.111 cm"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 1,
      "answerSource": "derived",
      "answerKeyRef": null,
      "explanation": "The biprism deviation is δ = (μ−1)A = 0.5 × (π/180) rad ≈ 0.00873 rad, so the virtual source separation is d = 2aδ ≈ 2 × 0.3 × 0.00873 ≈ 5.24 mm. With D = a + b = 1 m and λ = 6×10⁻⁷ m, β = λD/d ≈ 1.15×10⁻⁴ m ≈ 0.011 cm.",
